WEBVTT

00:00:01.970 --> 00:00:05.230
<i>Main is finally permitted to go back home,</i>

00:00:05.230 --> 00:00:08.290
<i>and swears to put even more of her 
heart and soul into bookmaking</i>

00:00:08.290 --> 00:00:10.460
<i>for the sake of her little 
brother Kamil, as well.</i>

00:00:11.850 --> 00:00:13.420
<i>Meanwhile...</i>

00:00:14.970 --> 00:00:21.250
The plan to kidnap the blue-robed apprentice 
priestess at the Spring Prayer has failed.

00:00:21.830 --> 00:00:25.960
That is truly unfortunate, Viscount Gerlach.

00:00:26.490 --> 00:00:32.830
I was quite hoping to have that commoner 
blue-robed apprentice priestess

00:00:32.830 --> 00:00:35.150
and Lord Ferdinand both suffer...

00:00:35.610 --> 00:00:39.840
Viscountess Dahldolf,
I understand how you feel.

00:00:40.330 --> 00:00:44.330
It is quite unfortunate to lose your 
son, Lord Schicicoza, in such a way.

00:00:47.360 --> 00:00:51.100
Not to mention, you managed to let 
half of the Devouring soldiers

00:00:51.100 --> 00:00:53.520
I lent you get eliminated.

00:00:54.790 --> 00:00:58.330
I'm terribly sorry, Count Bindewald.

00:00:58.330 --> 00:01:02.320
I'd rather get more troops 
from you than an apology.

00:01:02.720 --> 00:01:04.340
What do you mean?

00:01:04.680 --> 00:01:09.830
I'd like to buy that blue-robed 
apprentice priestess from you.

00:01:12.330 --> 00:01:15.970
We are aware of your request through 
Viscount Gerlach's letter.

00:01:16.250 --> 00:01:20.240
If I recall correctly, if an adoption 
is by a noble from another domain,

00:01:20.240 --> 00:01:23.970
we did not need permission 
from Aub Ehrenfest?

00:01:24.300 --> 00:01:30.220
Count Bindewald is a noble from the 
neighboring domain of Ahrensbach.

00:01:30.630 --> 00:01:32.690
Ahrensbach...

00:01:35.860 --> 00:01:38.720
I must say, this is a favorable deal.

00:01:39.110 --> 00:01:46.320
I'm sure that commoner blue-robed apprentice 
priestess is a thorn in your side as well.

00:01:46.530 --> 00:01:49.880
Lord Ferdinand declared before 
the knights that the apprentice priestess

00:01:49.880 --> 00:01:52.280
was under his protection. 
If she was sold off...

00:01:52.280 --> 00:01:56.150
I'm sure Lord Ferdinand 
would suffer, too.

00:01:59.580 --> 00:02:03.960
I'm certain that will make your older 
sister, Lady Veronica, happy, too.

00:02:03.960 --> 00:02:07.040
In order to find out more about this 
blue-robed apprentice priestess

00:02:07.040 --> 00:02:08.890
and what kind of contracts she may have,

00:02:08.890 --> 00:02:14.900
we were hoping we could get your assistance, 
since you are the high priest, Lord Bezewanst.

00:02:37.010 --> 00:02:40.510
<b>Ascendance of a Bookworm</b>

00:02:40.510 --> 00:02:42.020
<b>Ascendance of a Bookworm</b>

00:04:00.960 --> 00:04:05.970
<b>Chapter Thirty-Two</b>

00:04:00.960 --> 00:04:05.970
<b>The Abandoned Child of the Cathedral
 and Making Colors</b>

00:04:07.960 --> 00:04:11.880
My little brother Kamil is so adorable!

00:04:11.880 --> 00:04:14.190
He was just born, so he's so tiny,

00:04:14.190 --> 00:04:16.700
and whenever he cries, he 
gets so red and wrinkly.

00:04:19.400 --> 00:04:23.650
I never knew a little 
brother could be so cute.

00:04:23.890 --> 00:04:25.220
That's enough.

00:04:25.220 --> 00:04:28.130
I get enough of doting parents 
from being around Otto.

00:04:28.520 --> 00:04:31.840
What?! Missus. Corinna had her baby, then?

00:04:32.070 --> 00:04:35.950
At the end of winter.
 Her name is Renate.

00:04:36.330 --> 00:04:40.710
She'll be the Gilberta Company's heiress.
 I hope you'll look after her.

00:04:40.970 --> 00:04:46.100
You don't seem that excited, considering 
she's your precious heiress.

00:04:46.450 --> 00:04:50.560
Yes, because Otto is excited 
enough for the both of us.

00:04:52.760 --> 00:04:55.560
Renate's absolutely adorable, 
no matter what she does.

00:04:57.060 --> 00:04:59.950
Renate's absolutely adorable, 
no matter what she does.

00:04:59.950 --> 00:05:02.070
Stop playing with your food, dear.

00:05:02.320 --> 00:05:06.320
Thank goodness the Gilberta 
Company has Missus. Corinna.

00:05:06.320 --> 00:05:09.430
More importantly, hurry up and 
tell me about the printing.

00:05:09.430 --> 00:05:10.150
Right.

00:05:10.750 --> 00:05:15.530
The head priest has told me not to do 
any letterpress printing for a while.

00:05:17.400 --> 00:05:22.430
If we keep moving forward, the vested 
interest opposing us will be the nobility.

00:05:22.770 --> 00:05:25.360
A vested interest of nobles...

00:05:26.670 --> 00:05:28.920
Discretion is the better 
part of valor indeed.

00:05:29.230 --> 00:05:34.320
So I want to put everything into 
making picture books for a while.

00:05:35.880 --> 00:05:38.770
Everything? What are you plotting?

00:05:39.090 --> 00:05:43.370
First, I want to create some colored ink 
so we can add colors to the pictures.

00:05:43.370 --> 00:05:47.080
Second, improving our mimeograph technology.

00:05:47.310 --> 00:05:51.780
Colored ink and improving 
mimeograph technology?

00:05:52.010 --> 00:05:55.280
Yes, but we'll have to hurry and 
prepare, or we won't make it in time.

00:05:55.660 --> 00:05:58.000
In time? For what?

00:05:58.000 --> 00:06:03.050
Why, creating a picture book to go 
along with my precious Kamil's growth.

00:06:03.050 --> 00:06:05.850
I'm going to give this 
my all for Kamil's sake!

00:06:06.200 --> 00:06:08.840
Did you get permission from the head priest?

00:06:09.160 --> 00:06:11.230
If you did, that's fine.

00:06:11.230 --> 00:06:14.430
I'll let you meet the foreman 
of the workshop soon.

00:06:14.870 --> 00:06:16.740
Thank you kindly.

00:06:19.670 --> 00:06:23.510
My little brother was born the other day.

00:06:23.510 --> 00:06:25.270
Congratulations.

00:06:27.040 --> 00:06:30.030
Oh, I had no idea.

00:06:30.340 --> 00:06:34.030
<i>Oh, no. I was so excited that I let
 the cat out of the bag myself.</i>

00:06:34.390 --> 00:06:36.870
Lady Main, what's your brother's name?

00:06:37.200 --> 00:06:39.840
<i>Nice follow up, Gil! Yay!</i>

00:06:39.840 --> 00:06:41.840
His name is Kamil.

00:06:41.840 --> 00:06:44.420
He was just born, so he's really tiny.

00:06:44.420 --> 00:06:46.740
And when he cries, he gets 
all red and wrinkly.

00:06:46.740 --> 00:06:48.600
He's absolutely adorable!

00:06:48.600 --> 00:06:53.780
Lady Main, I must say, the way you describe 
him doesn't make him sound that cute.

00:06:56.990 --> 00:06:58.360
I wonder who that is.

00:07:00.320 --> 00:07:01.810
Pardon me.

00:07:03.680 --> 00:07:07.150
Wilma, where'd that baby come from?

00:07:07.640 --> 00:07:08.950
Well...

00:07:10.530 --> 00:07:12.430
I offer him to the gods.

00:07:13.720 --> 00:07:16.670
So she brought him here because 
she couldn't take care of him...

00:07:16.670 --> 00:07:19.840
Apparently so. What shall we do?

00:07:20.540 --> 00:07:23.000
What should we do?

00:07:24.230 --> 00:07:27.780
This is the first time I've dealt 
with something like this, too.

00:07:28.640 --> 00:07:33.710
<i>Fran requested a meeting with the head 
priest so we could talk to him about this.</i>

00:07:36.150 --> 00:07:38.230
He's so adorable.

00:07:38.480 --> 00:07:40.740
<i>He may be cute,</i>

00:07:40.740 --> 00:07:44.090
<i>but my Kamil's way cuter!</i>

00:07:44.400 --> 00:07:49.160
He's fine because he's sleeping right now, 
but what should we do when he wakes up?

00:07:49.160 --> 00:07:50.860
Give him milk.

00:07:50.860 --> 00:07:52.530
That's not possible.

00:07:52.530 --> 00:07:56.410
We don't have any gray-robed priestesses 
that have given birth left.

00:07:57.960 --> 00:08:04.050
Do you know anything about raising 
a baby without a mother, Lady Main?

00:08:04.050 --> 00:08:12.740
Well... I have read before that a mother who 
couldn't nurse gave their baby goat's milk.

00:08:12.740 --> 00:08:14.530
Goat's milk?

00:08:14.530 --> 00:08:18.040
Thank you kindly. I will 
prepare some right away.

00:08:21.840 --> 00:08:24.300
What should we do? He's crying.

00:08:30.460 --> 00:08:33.600
Judging by the way he's crying, he's hungry.

00:08:33.600 --> 00:08:35.810
I will go get some goat's milk.

00:08:35.810 --> 00:08:37.000
Ugh!

00:08:37.710 --> 00:08:39.070
He's wet.

00:08:39.070 --> 00:08:42.310
Oh, no! We need to change his diaper!

00:08:42.310 --> 00:08:43.380
Diaper...

00:08:43.380 --> 00:08:44.820
Do we have any cloth?

00:08:45.160 --> 00:08:46.820
Yes, we do.

00:08:48.870 --> 00:08:50.610
Hmm... an abandoned child.

00:08:51.310 --> 00:08:53.790
Just take care of him like you 
have done for the other children.

00:08:54.430 --> 00:08:59.670
We came to talk to you because none of the 
gray-robed priestesses have had a child.

00:09:00.160 --> 00:09:01.380
Right.

00:09:01.780 --> 00:09:04.810
But there's nothing we can do about that.

00:09:04.810 --> 00:09:06.370
Shall we hire a wet nurse?

00:09:07.400 --> 00:09:11.180
Sadly, I have no experience 
in child rearing as well.

00:09:11.610 --> 00:09:13.870
We can actually hire a wet nurse?

00:09:14.290 --> 00:09:18.350
If we can find anyone pious 
enough to come to the orphanage.

00:09:19.330 --> 00:09:22.110
That seems difficult.

00:09:27.050 --> 00:09:30.700
And so, we're all going 
to be taking care of him.

00:09:30.700 --> 00:09:32.040
All of us?!

00:09:32.040 --> 00:09:36.730
Yes. If Wilma has to take care of him 
herself, she's going to collapse,

00:09:36.730 --> 00:09:39.550
because babies need milk at night, too.

00:09:41.290 --> 00:09:44.310
Wilma will watch the child during the day,

00:09:44.310 --> 00:09:47.430
and the rest of you can take 
turns watching him at night.

00:09:47.730 --> 00:09:49.340
Understood.

00:09:49.340 --> 00:09:53.690
Ugh! Why do I have to do this, too?

00:09:53.940 --> 00:09:56.570
Of course, you should look after him.

00:09:56.570 --> 00:09:59.080
You're going to be this 
child's older sister.

00:09:59.340 --> 00:10:01.030
O-Older sister?

00:10:01.320 --> 00:10:06.290
Yes. I would like for you to care for this 
child like he's your own flesh and blood.

00:10:06.620 --> 00:10:09.880
<i>But my dream is to become a concubine!</i>

00:10:10.940 --> 00:10:13.410
<i>If she concentrates her 
attention somewhere else,</i>

00:10:13.410 --> 00:10:15.800
<i>she may forget about wanting 
to be a concubine!</i>

00:10:14.280 --> 00:10:15.800
<i>There, there!</i>

00:10:16.250 --> 00:10:19.930
Let's see who can be the better big sister.

00:10:20.170 --> 00:10:22.880
Well, of course I'm going to win.

00:10:23.150 --> 00:10:26.510
Delia, you always let Lady 
Main play you like a fiddle.

00:10:26.510 --> 00:10:27.880
Shut up.

00:10:27.880 --> 00:10:31.380
All right, first, let's 
give this child a name.

00:10:31.780 --> 00:10:34.600
In that case, I want his name
 to sound similar to mine.

00:10:34.600 --> 00:10:36.440
Then I might feel like he's my family.

00:10:36.440 --> 00:10:38.660
A name that sounds like Delia...

00:10:39.020 --> 00:10:40.210
Delia...

00:10:40.640 --> 00:10:47.530
Deita... Deetoria... Dil... Dirk...

00:10:47.840 --> 00:10:52.110
Dirk... Since he's a boy,
I think we should go with Dirk.

00:10:52.490 --> 00:10:55.130
Then Dirk it is.

00:10:55.130 --> 00:10:58.250
Your name is Dirk, little boy.

00:11:04.400 --> 00:11:06.180
He's crying.

00:11:06.430 --> 00:11:09.300
I'm sorry, Dirk. Please don't cry.

00:11:09.630 --> 00:11:12.010
Hello, Dirk.

00:11:12.510 --> 00:11:16.580
I'm going to be your big 
sister starting today.

00:11:19.150 --> 00:11:22.040
There, there. Good boy.

00:11:25.410 --> 00:11:29.240
Did you see that? Dirk smiled at me!

00:11:29.800 --> 00:11:33.000
Well, Lady Main has Master Kamil.

00:11:33.610 --> 00:11:37.400
Well, Kamil always cries at me, too.

00:11:40.010 --> 00:11:43.930
<b>Ascendance of a
 Bookworm</b>

00:11:46.090 --> 00:11:50.020
<b>Ascendance of a
 Bookworm</b>

00:11:52.800 --> 00:11:54.930
Kamil, it's your big sister.

00:12:03.910 --> 00:12:06.370
Jeez, why are you crying again?

00:12:06.370 --> 00:12:08.950
Aw, you made him cry again.

00:12:08.950 --> 00:12:12.510
Kamil always cries whenever 
he sees Main's face.

00:12:13.750 --> 00:12:17.770
We're actually going to be taking care of an 
abandoned baby at the orphanage now, too,

00:12:17.770 --> 00:12:19.830
and he also cried on me.

00:12:20.260 --> 00:12:22.220
What am I doing wrong?

00:12:22.480 --> 00:12:24.650
An abandoned baby? 
You're going to raise him?

00:12:24.650 --> 00:12:29.480
Yes. We're taking turns watching over 
him, so it's going to be rough.

00:12:29.480 --> 00:12:33.200
Then why don't you set a sleep 
schedule for them?

00:12:33.200 --> 00:12:36.470
Being able to nap will make 
your lives much easier.

00:12:36.740 --> 00:12:39.500
I see. Thanks, Mom.

00:12:40.950 --> 00:12:44.190
Kamil, well? Do you like picture books?

00:12:46.430 --> 00:12:49.210
Did you see that? Kamil didn't cry!

00:12:49.210 --> 00:12:50.630
He's looking at the picture book!

00:12:50.980 --> 00:12:53.060
I'd expect nothing less 
from my baby brother.

00:12:53.060 --> 00:12:57.680
Your sister is going to make a picture book 
with pretty colors next, so wait for me.

00:13:01.270 --> 00:13:03.310
She should be here any moment.

00:13:03.310 --> 00:13:04.460
Please excuse me.

00:13:06.770 --> 00:13:08.410
Dad, is that her?

00:13:08.410 --> 00:13:10.180
Don't point.

00:13:10.180 --> 00:13:12.690
Good morning, Lady Main.

00:13:14.910 --> 00:13:18.690
This is Bierce, the new 
head of the Ink Guild.

00:13:18.690 --> 00:13:23.200
About that... I'm the foreman 
of the ink workshop.

00:13:23.200 --> 00:13:25.940
I'm not fit to be the head of the Ink Guild.

00:13:26.980 --> 00:13:30.180
Not to mention, I have no idea 
how to deal with nobles.

00:13:30.180 --> 00:13:33.670
Boss, why don't you become 
the head of the Ink Guild?

00:13:33.670 --> 00:13:35.680
Don't make it sound so simple.

00:13:35.680 --> 00:13:39.340
I'm sure there will be plenty 
of nobles that will ask

00:13:39.340 --> 00:13:42.930
for the shady business dealings they had 
going on with Wolf to continue.

00:13:43.570 --> 00:13:50.170
If I end up selling ink, the guild master 
will try to give me even more trouble.

00:13:50.170 --> 00:13:54.940
I'd honestly feel much better if 
you sold the ink, Mister Benno.

00:13:55.360 --> 00:13:57.410
Do you want me to die from exhaustion?

00:13:57.650 --> 00:14:00.140
Well, I definitely can't do it.

00:14:02.820 --> 00:14:05.150
Why don't we ask the guild master's 
shop to take care of it?

00:14:05.150 --> 00:14:07.650
What? You're going to let 
someone else sell it?

00:14:07.650 --> 00:14:13.620
I would love to, but there was some 
merchandise that guild master was dealing

00:14:13.620 --> 00:14:16.670
that Wolf monopolized as soon as he 
became the head of the Ink Guild.

00:14:16.670 --> 00:14:19.170
What do you think will happen 
if I go to him again?

00:14:19.430 --> 00:14:24.180
I can only imagine. I can already 
hear that old geezer cackling.

00:14:27.130 --> 00:14:30.110
That's why I came to the 
Gilberta Company instead.

00:14:30.460 --> 00:14:32.690
Come on, help me out, miss.

00:14:32.690 --> 00:14:36.930
Sure, as long as you help me 
out in developing colored ink.

00:14:37.110 --> 00:14:38.340
Colored ink?

00:14:38.340 --> 00:14:39.570
Colored ink?

00:14:39.570 --> 00:14:40.990
Colored ink?

00:14:40.990 --> 00:14:44.690
Yes, colored ink. I'm about to invent it.

00:14:44.690 --> 00:14:48.070
Ooh! I'll do it! I wanna help!

00:14:48.070 --> 00:14:50.360
That's why I'm here!

00:14:52.490 --> 00:14:54.620
Um... and you are...?

00:14:54.620 --> 00:14:56.530
This is my daughter, Heidi.

00:14:56.530 --> 00:15:02.880
Her and her husband Josef are the ones 
making the ink you created for the plant paper.

00:15:02.880 --> 00:15:04.740
Oh, I see.

00:15:05.000 --> 00:15:10.500
The way you make ink is so new and 
different that it blew me away!

00:15:10.500 --> 00:15:12.080
I look forward to working with you!

00:15:12.580 --> 00:15:16.550
My name is Main. I look forward 
to working with you, as well.

00:15:18.940 --> 00:15:22.760
The reason I came here today is because 
I was thinking we could probably

00:15:22.760 --> 00:15:25.700
make plant-based ink in colors besides black.

00:15:25.700 --> 00:15:28.280
We absolutely can! Please go for it!

00:15:28.630 --> 00:15:30.530
Do you know what would 
be the best ingredients?

00:15:30.850 --> 00:15:32.080
Well...

00:15:32.080 --> 00:15:32.850
Lady Main...

00:15:35.140 --> 00:15:37.370
I do have information on the ingredients.

00:15:37.370 --> 00:15:40.270
Once they're on the market,
 I'll be taking part of the sales

00:15:40.270 --> 00:15:42.000
as a fee for the information.

00:15:42.000 --> 00:15:46.410
That's too expensive! It costs so 
much to get something to the market.

00:15:47.100 --> 00:15:50.370
In that case... I'll take care of 
half of your initial expenses.

00:15:50.370 --> 00:15:51.850
A quarter is more than enough.

00:15:52.220 --> 00:15:53.790
Sounds fair to me.

00:15:54.090 --> 00:15:57.840
You've got a deal. Want to head 
over to the workshop right now?

00:15:57.840 --> 00:16:00.900
I collected a bunch of ingredients 
I thought might work.

00:16:00.900 --> 00:16:03.150
That sounds wonderful! I'd love to go!

00:16:07.840 --> 00:16:09.450
Calm down, you fool!

00:16:09.450 --> 00:16:11.230
We haven't finished talking yet!

00:16:15.840 --> 00:16:17.710
I'm gonna go ahead and get things ready.

00:16:18.450 --> 00:16:22.860
Lutz, keep an eye on her. It's basically
 like we have two Mains now.

00:16:22.860 --> 00:16:27.320
You can't be serious, Master. My 
hands are already full with this Main.

00:16:27.700 --> 00:16:32.420
Say, Lutz. Heidi seems interesting and
 really passionate about her work,

00:16:32.420 --> 00:16:34.100
but she's also... <i>unique</i>.

00:16:34.530 --> 00:16:36.400
You should be the last person to say that.

00:16:41.060 --> 00:16:43.600
Sure, that's fine.

00:16:44.180 --> 00:16:45.820
Hello!

00:16:46.910 --> 00:16:49.140
Hey, Miss! Over here!

00:16:53.300 --> 00:16:56.040
The best kind of oil to use 
when making ink is drying oil.

00:16:56.040 --> 00:16:58.520
It's a type of oil that hardens when dried.

00:16:58.520 --> 00:17:03.040
So we'd be using linseed, mische, 
ped, eise, and turm oils.

00:17:05.710 --> 00:17:09.620
Then we'd just mix in 
some ground-up minerals.

00:17:09.620 --> 00:17:13.070
Okay, let's give it a try.
 Josef, help me out.

00:17:13.070 --> 00:17:13.900
Right.

00:17:14.370 --> 00:17:16.100
This is my husband.

00:17:16.100 --> 00:17:18.690
It's nice to meet you. My name is Main.

00:17:18.690 --> 00:17:21.430
I'm in charge of the Main Workshop.

00:17:21.430 --> 00:17:22.530
I'm Josef.

00:17:22.530 --> 00:17:26.470
Today, I've come here to purchase 
some ink for plant paper,

00:17:26.470 --> 00:17:30.530
and I wanted to be here to see 
you make new colors for the ink.

00:17:30.750 --> 00:17:33.850
S-Sure. Pleasure to have you.

00:17:34.890 --> 00:17:36.530
Thank you.

00:17:36.840 --> 00:17:39.360
Which things did you want to mix, miss?

00:17:39.610 --> 00:17:41.280
Well...

00:17:41.570 --> 00:17:45.090
If you mix that yellow 
clay with the linseed oil,

00:17:45.090 --> 00:17:48.250
you should end up with a color 
in between yellow and brown.

00:17:48.650 --> 00:17:49.750
You got it!

00:17:59.550 --> 00:18:01.100
That's strange...

00:18:01.100 --> 00:18:02.850
That's definitely not brown.

00:18:03.130 --> 00:18:04.480
But why...

00:18:06.820 --> 00:18:08.090
It turned blue.

00:18:08.950 --> 00:18:10.640
Let's try some mische.

00:18:18.270 --> 00:18:19.700
Next, some ped.

00:18:22.270 --> 00:18:23.720
Bluish green.

00:18:24.910 --> 00:18:26.090
Next, eise.

00:18:29.990 --> 00:18:31.460
Ocher!

00:18:31.460 --> 00:18:33.510
We finally got the color we wanted.

00:18:36.000 --> 00:18:40.520
I never thought the different kinds of 
oils would produce different colors.

00:18:42.220 --> 00:18:44.280
Why does this happen?

00:18:48.960 --> 00:18:51.970
You're wondering that, too, 
right? Isn't it strange?!

00:18:51.970 --> 00:18:53.850
You totally want to find out why, right?!

00:18:53.850 --> 00:18:56.240
That doesn't really matter right now.

00:18:56.240 --> 00:18:59.570
What's important right now 
is what colors we can make.

00:18:59.760 --> 00:19:05.540
What?! You're not curious as
to why this mystery happens, Miss?

00:19:06.160 --> 00:19:10.420
Come on! Don't lump the young 
lady into your weirdo circle.

00:19:10.420 --> 00:19:12.300
That's so mean!

00:19:12.300 --> 00:19:15.410
I just thought we'd be able 
to understand each other...

00:19:15.970 --> 00:19:17.760
<i>Understand each other?</i>

00:19:18.730 --> 00:19:22.360
I'd like to know the results 
rather than the hows and whys.

00:19:22.870 --> 00:19:26.200
And I was able to get the 
color I wanted with eise.

00:19:26.900 --> 00:19:31.010
Next... let's try that blue and some eise.

00:19:37.210 --> 00:19:39.120
This time, it turned yellow.

00:19:39.120 --> 00:19:41.690
This may be more difficult than I thought.

00:19:41.930 --> 00:19:43.780
This is work that's definitely worth doing.

00:19:45.010 --> 00:19:47.440
We need to sort out our results.

00:19:47.740 --> 00:19:51.910
Yes, but it's problematic that we can't 
anticipate how the colors will turn out.

00:19:54.400 --> 00:19:56.010
What is it, Gil?

00:19:58.280 --> 00:20:01.350
Lady Main, my writing board...

00:20:02.730 --> 00:20:05.790
I promised I'd get you one in spring.

00:20:07.800 --> 00:20:10.760
You did do your best to learn the alphabet.

00:20:11.070 --> 00:20:14.480
I'll ask Johann to make you a stylus.

00:20:20.170 --> 00:20:23.210
Thank you kindly, Lady Main.

00:20:28.750 --> 00:20:30.840
So that creature now has a little brother.

00:20:30.840 --> 00:20:31.660
Yes.

00:20:34.060 --> 00:20:36.740
I guess that doesn't really 
matter at this point.

00:20:36.740 --> 00:20:37.820
Huh?

00:20:38.260 --> 00:20:40.160
Any other changes to report?

00:20:40.510 --> 00:20:43.170
Changes?

00:20:43.620 --> 00:20:44.930
Um...

00:20:46.560 --> 00:20:49.040
There's a new orphan at the orphanage!

00:20:50.240 --> 00:20:52.000
You may take your leave now.

00:20:52.580 --> 00:20:56.630
Ugh... I thought I'd finally 
get a reward today.

00:21:00.040 --> 00:21:01.680
It'll be nice and warm soon.

00:21:01.680 --> 00:21:03.260
Thanks, Ella.

00:21:07.350 --> 00:21:09.540
Yes, yes. I'll be right there.

00:21:10.150 --> 00:21:11.830
Sorry to keep you waiting, Dirk.

00:21:12.660 --> 00:21:13.900
Dirk...

00:21:17.610 --> 00:21:18.710
Dirk!

00:21:19.480 --> 00:21:21.820
What are these spots?

00:21:22.270 --> 00:21:23.730
He feels so hot...

00:21:23.940 --> 00:21:26.320
What a terrible fever... but why?

00:21:28.700 --> 00:21:29.960
Dirk...

00:23:04.940 --> 00:23:07.950
<b>Next Chapter
Delia and Dirk</b>

00:23:09.800 --> 00:23:12.370
Hey! Dirk is crying!

00:23:12.370 --> 00:23:14.630
I'll sing him a lullaby.

00:23:14.630 --> 00:23:18.570
Fall asleep, fall asleep, 
fall asleep, fall asleep...

00:23:18.570 --> 00:23:21.880
Rosina, you just want an excuse to 
play the harspiel. There, there.

00:23:21.880 --> 00:23:23.870
Oh, that'll make a lovely painting.

00:23:23.870 --> 00:23:27.060
If you're going to paint, paint Dirk and I.

00:23:29.300 --> 00:23:34.540
So... Taking care of Dirk 
is going well... I guess?

00:23:34.970 --> 00:23:39.970
Illustration by: keepout
